STATES  (every branch the WEB SOURCE actually has — reproduced; none hidden)
  dismissed → already onboarded, not yet revealed, or dismissed by a peer scene → renders nothing (web
              `if (!visible) return null`). This is the sanctioned "withdrawn surface" disposition (identical to the
              AiUsageCard off-mode gate), NOT a hidden-when-null data section.
  presented → the blurred backdrop + the centered card for steps[currentStep], with the indicator row + Skip +
              Next/Get-Started + ✕, across all four steps (step content, the Next→Get-Started transition on the last
              step, and the indicator completion all rendered + tested).
  NB: OnboardingWizard is a PURE presentational component with NO data feed (the prompt's "Data sources: none").
      It therefore has no loading / error / stale / offline axis — the generic state list in the prompt template is a
      data-surface checklist; fabricating those states for a feed-less wizard would MISREPRESENT the source. The
      operative instruction ("plus any state-specific branches that exist in the web source — reproduce them all") is
      honoured: dismissed + presented(×4 steps) are the web's real branches and all render.

